Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: libtiff/tif_dirread.c
Line: 2837
Function: TIFFReadDirEntryFloatArray
Bug type: heap-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-122
Explanation: Allocates data with size count * sizeof(float) without checking for size_t overflow. On 32-bit platforms, count * 4 can overflow, producing an undersized buffer. The following loops write count float elements into data (e.g., at lines 2852–2853, 2863–2864, 2873–2879, 2888–2894, 2903–2909, 2918–2924, 2933–2939, 2948–2954, 2965–2978, 2990–3000), causing heap buffer overflow.

Source context:
```c
